[h1]Overview:[/h1]
Allows you to rename any country (even yourself).

[h1]Features:[/h1]
[olist]
 [*][b]Rename any country:[/b] Rename any country, including your own, via the right-click context menu.
 [*][b]Optional country title:[/b] Tick the "Show country title" checkbox in the rename dialog to keep the country's normal title formatting on the new name, for example "Kingdom of Gaul" instead of just "Gaul". Leave it unchecked to display the name exactly as typed.
[/olist]

[h1]Note:[/h1]
[olist]
 [*] You may have to wait a couple of months to see updated names reflected on the map. Saving and reloading may speed this up.
 [*] The mod does not currently work in multiplayer. I have not found a good workaround yet. There is one possible way that is pretty terrible to do, but if anyone knows a workaround or wants to implement my wacky solution, reach out and I will add you to the mod page as well.
[/olist]

[h1]Native Localizations:[/h1]
[list]
 [*][b]English:[/b] Primary
 [*][b]Polish / Polski:[/b] Thanks to @kacpi_tv.
 [*][b]Chinese (中文):[/b] Available in the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3599706198]凯撒汉化 (Caesar Chinese Translation) mod[/url].
[/list]

[h1]DeepL-Translated Localizations:[/h1]
[list]
 [*][b]French / Français[/b]
 [*][b]German / Deutsch[/b]
 [*][b]Japanese / 日本語[/b]
 [*][b]Korean / 한국어[/b]
 [*][b]Portuguese (Brazil) / Português (Brasil)[/b]
